1
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:24,260
Anyone who's broke, come to me!

2
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:28,980
Not that I have any either, so don't worry.

3
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:36,020
Look at that blue sky, those white clouds.

4
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:54,460
The world's biggest sporting event

5
00:01:54,460 --> 00:01:56,140
World Cup soccer

6
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:58,380
has finally come to Japan!

7
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:11,620
In the second semifinal match of the World
Cup One-Day Police Station Soccer Tournament,

8
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:14,760
Katsushika A Team wins with a golden goal!

9
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:17,160
So you did show up, Kankichi Ryotsu.

10
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:20,340
You'll make a fine opponent in the final.

11
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:22,980
You'd better be ready for me, Komachi.

12
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:24,320
You're one to talk!

13
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:29,460
Next week's final will pit
Ono Komachi's Katsushika B Team

14
00:02:29,460 --> 00:02:34,140
against Kankichi Ryotsu's Katsushika A Team.

15
00:02:36,020 --> 00:02:40,360
I have some happy news. It's sudden,
but the winning team of this tournament

16
00:02:40,360 --> 00:02:44,560
will be receiving World Cup final tickets.

17
00:02:47,220 --> 00:02:48,980
Did I say something strange?

18
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:53,240
No, I only said we'd be giving
away World Cup final tickets...

19
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:56,000
World Cup final tickets!

20
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:56,320
Aargh!

21
00:03:01,900 --> 00:03:05,600
World Cup tickets are super platinum paper,
you know.

22
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:08,200
Even Nakagawa can't get them easily.

23
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:10,860
Hundreds of millions of people want them.

24
00:03:12,420 --> 00:03:14,380
I had no idea they were that hard to get.

25
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:18,640
I'll definitely get tickets
to the World Cup final.

26
00:03:20,760 --> 00:03:23,160
2,000 street soccer players.

27
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:31,180
The day of the World Cup commemorative police
station soccer tournament final has finally arrived.

28
00:03:31,820 --> 00:03:35,500
Here comes the Katsushika A team,
led by Kankichi Ryotsu.

29
00:03:36,140 --> 00:03:37,820
No, no, ice cream.

30
00:03:37,820 --> 00:03:40,360
What's that?

31
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:44,760
No way, no way, it's definitely them!

32
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:47,600
They're players who star in
South American pro leagues!

33
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:52,720
Top pros from the countries that were knocked out in qualifiers and couldn't make the World Cup,
all assembled!

34
00:03:53,160 --> 00:03:55,500
I don't want you to get the wrong idea.

35
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:59,500
They're people who came to Katsushika
Station as trainee police officers.

36
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:02,560
Well, they may have some soccer skills,
I suppose.

37
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:04,940
The Katsushika B team has arrived.

38
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:08,020
Here they come,
not knowing they're going to lose.

39
00:04:08,020 --> 00:04:13,080
Wait, those are players who
star in European pro leagues!

40
00:04:13,560 --> 00:04:14,140
What?

41
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:19,480
These people came to the Traffic
Division as relatives of a trainee.

42
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:21,580
They can play soccer a little, too.

43
00:04:23,780 --> 00:04:26,600
I had them come just in case
something like this happened.

44
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:28,520
Now the teams are evenly matched.

45
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:30,940
Damn it, Reiko's doing?

46
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:34,240
With both teams bringing in
super-powerful reinforcements,

47
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:37,020
it's starting to look
like a shadow World Cup.

48
00:04:45,880 --> 00:04:47,580
We've just received word.

49
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:51,460
Apparently the ground made
a double booking by mistake.

50
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:55,980
We're urgently looking
for another ground, but

51
00:04:55,980 --> 00:05:00,360
they're all taken, so it looks
like today's match can't go ahead.

52
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:04,800
Then what's going to happen
to the World Cup final tickets?

53
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:07,640
Maybe they could decide it by
rock-paper-scissors or something.

54
00:05:07,640 --> 00:05:09,180
Don't be ridiculous.

55
00:05:09,180 --> 00:05:13,480
We didn't bring in ringers all the way from South
America just so they could play rock-paper-scissors!

56
00:05:13,880 --> 00:05:15,260
The same goes for us!

57
00:05:15,260 --> 00:05:16,560
But...

58
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:21,200
Now that you mention it,
the 6-chome ground was free, wasn't it?

59
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:21,920
Really?

60
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:28,380
Isn't it too small after all?

61
00:05:29,440 --> 00:05:30,820
Please look over there.

62
00:05:30,820 --> 00:05:32,640
That's the 7-chome ground.

63
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:36,980
Put together, they're about the
size of a regular soccer pitch.

64
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:38,840
W-wait, you mean both of them?

65
00:05:38,840 --> 00:05:39,940
Exactly.

66
00:05:39,940 --> 00:05:42,740
We're going to play the match
using both of these grounds.

67
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:45,920
That's crazy, Ryo-chan.

68
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:47,940
There's a road right in between them.

69
00:05:47,940 --> 00:05:49,780
We can't possibly play a match like that.

70
00:05:49,780 --> 00:05:52,700
Honestly,
we could just forfeit the match, you know.

71
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:54,920
Then the tickets would be ours,
wouldn't they?

72
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:57,620
Nobody said we weren't going to play.

73
00:05:58,140 --> 00:05:59,780
Alright, then it's settled.

74
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:04,220
The venue has been hastily moved
to the 6-chome and 7-chome grounds,

75
00:06:04,220 --> 00:06:09,680
and the police station World Cup commemorative
soccer final is about to finally begin.

76
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:11,720
Let's go!

77
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:15,320
Both teams dash toward the
6-chome ground at full speed.

78
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:16,780
You're not getting through here!

79
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:19,040
Can you stop me?

80
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:23,300
A long shot!

81
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:29,100
Yay!

82
00:06:29,100 --> 00:06:31,120
Otachi team scores first!

83
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:33,940
The match has only just begun.

84
00:06:38,620 --> 00:06:40,540
The same attack pattern again.

85
00:06:40,540 --> 00:06:41,520
That was too high.

86
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:49,120
Damn it.

87
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:52,200
Go, Honda!

88
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:53,560
Well, but...

89
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:54,557
Player Honda,

90
00:06:54,607 --> 00:06:58,100
is blocked by a red light
and can't move forward!

91
00:06:58,820 --> 00:06:59,620
Saved!

92
00:06:59,920 --> 00:07:02,040
Worst possible timing!

93
00:07:14,060 --> 00:07:17,040
The light's changing!
Everyone, get off the crosswalk!

94
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:17,660
Yes!

95
00:07:20,020 --> 00:07:20,860
What about the ball?

96
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:22,780
Don't leave the ball behind!

97
00:07:24,160 --> 00:07:25,200
Yay!

98
00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:35,040
It's impossible to hold
the match here after all.

99
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:36,520
Let's call it off.

100
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:39,320
I agree. But what about the result?

101
00:07:40,180 --> 00:07:41,760
Obviously, we win!

102
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:44,080
Because we're one point ahead!

103
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:44,700
Hey.

104
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:46,220
No way, that's ridiculous!

105
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:48,160
The match has only just started.

106
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:49,680
We should play it out to the end.

107
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:53,820
But there's no place to play!

108
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:58,720
But didn't people in the old
days play soccer without a ground?

109
00:07:59,320 --> 00:08:01,500
They were talking about
it on TV the other day.

110
00:08:02,020 --> 00:08:06,160
that soccer began as people
kicking a ball from town to town.

111
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:09,580
Then let's recreate that, shall we?

112
00:08:09,580 --> 00:08:11,740
We'll play soccer right through the town!

113
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:14,440
No, no, no way!

114
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:17,480
If we did that,
we'd be causing trouble for the townspeople.

115
00:08:19,820 --> 00:08:20,540
Chief

116
00:08:20,540 --> 00:08:23,020
Chief, you always say we
must cherish tradition.

117
00:08:23,020 --> 00:08:26,120
You're always telling us to
respect traditional culture, right?

118
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:31,640
Then shouldn't we respect
the tradition of soccer too?

119
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:35,860
The tradition of soccer is,
in other words, street soccer.

120
00:08:35,860 --> 00:08:39,980
How can Japan call itself a World Cup
host nation if it doesn't allow this?

121
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:45,700
I'll be careful not to inconvenience
the townspeople as much as possible.

122
00:08:46,260 --> 00:08:48,900
But what matters even more is

123
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:51,380
holding street soccer right here,

124
00:08:51,380 --> 00:08:54,500
and showing the world

125
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:57,300
how much Japan respects
the tradition of soccer.

126
00:09:00,860 --> 00:09:03,360
Something feels like I'm being tricked, but

127
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:05,780
In the end, we just have to win on skill.

128
00:09:05,780 --> 00:09:07,820
Alright, the match is back on!

129
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:13,100
The World Cup commemorative police station
soccer tournament final

130
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:15,260
has changed venues again.

131
00:09:15,820 --> 00:09:18,220
Komachi team's goal is the station plaza.

132
00:09:18,220 --> 00:09:21,380
Ryotsu's team's goal is the
children's park in 3-chome.

133
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:24,680
The whole town will become the soccer field.

134
00:09:24,680 --> 00:09:25,700
Let's go!

135
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:28,240
I'll take it, thanks!

136
00:09:28,730 --> 00:09:29,340
Take it!

137
00:09:31,720 --> 00:09:33,340
Damn, into the back alleys

138
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:34,600
Here he comes.

139
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:35,720
Kora-chan

140
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:44,960
Those big traffic-jam guys must find it hard to move
in the narrow back alleys of the old town, right?

141
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:55,040
Whoa, what's going on?

142
00:09:55,040 --> 00:09:59,680
Even top-class pro soccer players
are at a loss in Tokyo's old downtown.

143
00:10:00,740 --> 00:10:01,540
Found him.

144
00:10:01,540 --> 00:10:02,800
Looks like we lost sight of him.

145
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:05,960
This area is like a backyard to Ryo-chan.

146
00:10:06,420 --> 00:10:08,360
Damn it, Kankichi Ryotsu!

147
00:10:09,860 --> 00:10:11,000
Leave it to me.

148
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:15,760
Nobody's following us

149
00:10:15,760 --> 00:10:18,620
Alright,
I'll charge straight to the goal from here.

150
00:10:18,620 --> 00:10:21,120
Found you, Kankichi Ryotsu!

151
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:21,440
What?

152
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:24,300
I won't let you have your way.

153
00:10:25,340 --> 00:10:26,240
Komachi!

154
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:31,520
A player on the rooftop!

155
00:10:31,820 --> 00:10:32,580
What?!

156
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:34,620
It's a counter!

157
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:37,060
Everyone, get up on the roofs, quick!

158
00:10:37,140 --> 00:10:39,560
Organized soccer, just like Europe!

159
00:10:39,560 --> 00:10:41,120
Skillfully linking pass after pass!

160
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:43,120
Anyone, stop him!

161
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:47,300
Two ahead at the corner!

162
00:10:47,820 --> 00:10:49,500
Well done, Sensō-ji!

163
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:52,120
Another kid?

164
00:10:52,360 --> 00:10:53,360
Komachi-dah!

165
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:05,920
It's like a spin ball!

166
00:11:05,920 --> 00:11:07,380
Nothing's going my way.

167
00:11:07,380 --> 00:11:08,860
Nakagawa, pass!

168
00:11:08,860 --> 00:11:11,520
Offside!

169
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:12,840
What?!

170
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:16,940
The enemy goal is to the north-northeast,
so that pass was offside.

171
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:18,800
Come on, even your right-hand man...

172
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:21,380
You're sure the encirclement is right,
aren't you?

173
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:27,000
Excuse me, this is for the repairs.

174
00:11:27,680 --> 00:11:30,000
What kind of group are you people?

175
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:33,740
One-on-one with the keeper!
What a perfect chance!

176
00:11:33,900 --> 00:11:34,620
Tug!

177
00:11:35,060 --> 00:11:37,200
Damn, at this rate they'll score!

178
00:11:38,420 --> 00:11:39,880
Komachi, get ready to shoot!

179
00:11:40,180 --> 00:11:41,260
Got it!

180
00:11:42,260 --> 00:11:43,000
That's enough!

181
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:47,020
Sorry, I mistook the ball

182
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:48,780
That's dirty!

183
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:53,480
The ball goes to the bargain venue

184
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:56,140
Don't take it from me

185
00:11:56,140 --> 00:11:57,260
Stop it, which one?

186
00:12:06,680 --> 00:12:08,940
I ended up falling into a manhole.

187
00:12:11,820 --> 00:12:13,420
Where's the ball? Where's the ball?

188
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:15,560
Wait!

189
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:16,800
Hold on!

190
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:19,520
Okay!

191
00:12:20,740 --> 00:12:21,160
Yes!

192
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:22,120
Now!

193
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:24,160
Whoa! I got it!

194
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:28,340
Yes! It's a tie!

195
00:12:29,380 --> 00:12:31,280
What are you doing, Ryo-chan?

196
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:31,690
Senpai,

197
00:12:31,740 --> 00:12:35,580
the first half ended long
ago and it's halftime already.

198
00:12:36,460 --> 00:12:38,700
We blew the whistle many times.

199
00:12:38,700 --> 00:12:41,580
Senpai, you were underground,
so you couldn't hear it

200
00:12:43,060 --> 00:12:45,420
After all that effort to get this far...

201
00:12:45,420 --> 00:12:48,100
No wonder nobody was chasing me.

202
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:49,480
How stupid.

203
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:50,440
Hehe.

204
00:13:01,420 --> 00:13:05,160
Now, the final of the World Cup
Commemorative Police Station Soccer Tournament!

205
00:13:05,160 --> 00:13:07,060
It's the second-half kickoff.

206
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:10,440
Right at the start of the second half,

207
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:12,560
Team Komachi is launching a fierce attack!

208
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:15,120
We need to shore up the goal!

209
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:23,300
Oh no, this girl's going to get beaten!

210
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:28,360
The ball is flying toward the
top right corner of the goal.

211
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:30,380
Is that Team Komachi's second goal?

212
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:31,960
Not if I can help it!

213
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:39,000
It missed the goal!

214
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:42,340
That's unfair, moving the goals like that!

215
00:13:42,340 --> 00:13:43,680
Yeah, that's right!

216
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:44,840
What are you talking about?

217
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:47,020
Keeping the goals movable is

218
00:13:47,020 --> 00:13:49,960
basic courtesy in street soccer!

219
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:51,820
Courtesy? Where exactly?

220
00:13:51,820 --> 00:13:53,680
Street soccer is

221
00:13:53,680 --> 00:13:59,800
the stage for residents' lives. Of course, there
are people who go about their normal work too.

222
00:13:59,800 --> 00:14:05,440
For those people, the goals must always be movable.
Now that you mention it,

223
00:14:05,440 --> 00:14:13,060
there's some truth to that. Put the other way,
in street soccer, movable goals are common sense.

224
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:16,740
But if that's the case,
then goal areas and penalty areas

225
00:14:16,740 --> 00:14:18,540
can be ignored, right?

226
00:14:24,440 --> 00:14:26,780
Right, let's move the goals!

227
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,200
Wait!

228
00:14:29,200 --> 00:14:31,060
Both teams' goals are moving!

229
00:14:31,060 --> 00:14:32,940
Komachi team, after them!

230
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:36,120
Wait!

231
00:14:42,060 --> 00:14:43,780
Komachi, over there!

232
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:46,680
The enemy's tired, this is our chance!

233
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:47,780
Go!

234
00:14:48,960 --> 00:14:49,800
Chance!

235
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:54,640
If they fall for it,

236
00:14:56,340 --> 00:14:57,140
Now!

237
00:14:57,140 --> 00:14:58,580
Fururi, furifuri -

238
00:14:59,120 --> 00:14:59,740
Here it comes!

239
00:15:00,820 --> 00:15:02,620
That's our team's goal!

240
00:15:05,340 --> 00:15:07,020
Own goal!

241
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,500
Both teams have finally
caught up to tie the score.

242
00:15:12,980 --> 00:15:14,460
What a match.

243
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:16,620
This isn't even soccer anymore.

244
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:18,860
Run for it!

245
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:20,960
This is seriously good.

246
